# Trivy exceptions. JUSTIFIED EXCEPTIONS ONLY: fixing the finding always comes first. An exception is
# allowed when there is no fix, or the fix needs a major upgrade of upstream code, and the finding isn't
# reachable in our deployment. Accepted by a reviewer other than the proposer (the PR approval).
# Format: one ID per line, with an expiry:   <ID> exp:YYYY-MM-DD
# Every entry needs a comment above it: why, who accepted it, Jira ticket.
# After the expiry date the entry stops working and the gate fails again.
#
# Example for a CVE with no fix yet:
# Not reachable because <reason>. Accepted: <name>, SCRUM-<n>.
# CVE-YYYY-NNNNN exp:2026-12-31

# CVE-2026-47884 (CRITICAL): spring-webmvc 6.2.19, in ledgerwriter, balancereader, transactionhistory.
# SSRF/RCE in Spring MVC's XsltView, only when an app renders views through XsltView with a catch-all
# mapping and no explicit view name. Not reachable here: all three services are @RestController JSON
# APIs with explicit mappings; none uses XsltView, a ViewResolver or any server-side view (checked
# with grep over src/ledger). The only fix is Spring 7 (Spring Boot 4), a major upgrade of unmodified
# upstream code. Revisit when upstream Bank of Anthos moves to Spring Boot 4, or at the expiry.
# Proposed: yqyeoh. Accepted: paulyapsl (DevSecOps), SCRUM-37.
CVE-2026-47884 exp:2026-12-31

# CVE-2025-68121 (CRITICAL): Go stdlib crypto/tls certificate validation, in /usr/local/bin/gosu inside
# the accounts-db and ledger-db images (postgres:16.15-alpine's gosu 1.19 is built with Go 1.24.6).
# Not reachable here: these images only run our DB init Job, whose command (bash -c, then psql) replaces
# the image's entrypoint, so gosu never runs; and gosu makes no TLS connections. Fixed when the
# postgres image ships gosu built with Go >= 1.24.13. Proposed: yqyeoh. Accepted: paulyapsl (DevSecOps), SCRUM-37.
CVE-2025-68121 exp:2026-12-31

# CVE-2026-47890 (CRITICAL per NVD; Red Hat rates it 6.5 Medium): spring-webmvc 6.2.19, in ledgerwriter,
# balancereader, transactionhistory. Stream corruption when an endpoint renders view fragments over
# Server-Sent Events. Not reachable here: the services return plain JSON from @RestController methods;
# none uses SseEmitter, text/event-stream, fragment rendering or any server-side view (checked with
# grep over src/ledger). The only fix is Spring 7 (Spring Boot 4), the same major upgrade as
# CVE-2026-47884 above. Proposed: yqyeoh. Accepted: paulyapsl (DevSecOps), SCRUM-37.
CVE-2026-47890 exp:2026-12-31
